    <main class="col-md-9 col-xl-10 py-md-3 pl-md-5 bd-content">
      <div class="docs-section" id="getting-started">
        <h1>Getting Started
        <p class="lead">Learn how to install, configure, and start using Haskell Gerrit.

        <h2 id="installation">Installation</h2>
        <p>Follow these steps to install Haskell Gerrit:

        <div class="docs-code">
          <pre><code class="language-bash">
# Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/your-org/haskell-gerrit.git

# Install dependencies
cabal update
cabal build

# Set up the database
createdb haskell-gerrit
cabal run migrate

# Start the server
cabal run haskell-gerrit
          </code></pre>

        <h2 id="configuration">Configuration</h2>
        <p>Configure your instance by editing the following files:

        <div class="card mb-4">
          <div class="card-header">
            <code>config/development.env</code>
          <div class="card-body">
            <pre><code class="language-ini">
# Database configuration
GERRIT_DB_HOST=localhost
GERRIT_DB_NAME=gerrit
GERRIT_DB_USER=gerrit
GERRIT_DB_PASS=gerrit_password

# Server configuration
GERRIT_PORT=8080
GERRIT_GIT_PATH=/var/lib/gerrit/git
            </code></pre>

        <h2 id="first-steps">First Steps</h2>
        <p>After installation, follow these steps to get started:
        <ol>
          <li>Create an administrator account
          <li>Set up your first project
          <li>Configure user access
          <li>Create your first change

      <div class="docs-section" id="user-guide">
        <h1>User Guide
        <p class="lead">Learn how to use Haskell Gerrit effectively.

        <h2 id="creating-changes">Creating Changes</h2>
        <p>To create a new change:
        <ol>
          <li>Clone the project repository
          <li>Create a new branch
          <li>Make your changes
          <li>Push to Gerrit for review

        <div class="docs-code">
          <pre><code class="language-bash">
git clone http://gerrit.example.com/project
git checkout -b feature-branch
# Make changes
git add .
git commit -m "feat: add new feature"
git push origin HEAD:refs/for/master
          </code></pre>

        <h2 id="reviewing-code">Reviewing Code</h2>
        <p>Code review best practices:
        <ul>
          <li>Review changes thoroughly
          <li>Use inline comments for specific feedback
          <li>Test changes locally when necessary
          <li>Provide constructive feedback

        <h2 id="managing-projects">Managing Projects</h2>
        <p>Project management guidelines:
        <ul>
          <li>Set up proper access rights
          <li>Configure submit requirements
          <li>Manage project branches
          <li>Monitor project activity

      <div class="docs-section" id="api-reference">
        <h1>API Reference
        <p class="lead">Complete reference for the Haskell Gerrit REST API.

        <h2 id="authentication">Authentication</h2>
        <p>All API requests require authentication using JWT tokens.

        <div class="docs-code">
          <pre><code class="language-bash">
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
     https://gerrit.example.com/api/changes
          </code></pre>

        <h2 id="changes-api">Changes API</h2>
        <div class="api-endpoint">
          <h4>GET /changes</h4>
          <p>List all changes
          <h5>Parameters</h5>
          <table class="table table-sm">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Name</th>
                <th>Type</th>
                <th>Description</th>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>q</td>
                <td>string</td>
                <td>Search query</td>
              <tr>
                <td>n</td>
                <td>integer</td>
                <td>Number of changes to return</td>

        <h2 id="projects-api">Projects API</h2>
        <div class="api-endpoint">
          <h4>GET /projects</h4>
          <p>List all projects
          <h5>Parameters</h5>
          <table class="table table-sm">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Name</th>
                <th>Type</th>
                <th>Description</th>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>prefix</td>
                <td>string</td>
                <td>Filter projects by name prefix</td>
              <tr>
                <td>limit</td>
                <td>integer</td>
                <td>Maximum number of projects to return</td>

